2186414753 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c7bb7823-c38b-5250-a2f7-3b306162dae1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414753 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's denote \n\n$\\,$ ${a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$ \n\nWe proceed to find an orthogonal basis using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows.\n\n**Step 1**: We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n**Step 2**: Next, we find ${v}_{2}$, by using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for ${v}_{2}$ in our case gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{3\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 1+2\\cdot (-2)}{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{6}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{17}{6} \\\\ \\frac{11}{6} \\\\ \\frac{7}{3}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $B={{v}_{1},{v}_{2}}={\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{17}{6} \\\\ \\frac{11}{6} \\\\ \\frac{7}{3}\\end{bmatrix}}$ is an orthogonal basis for $V.$\n\nFinally, we have $a=\\frac{17}{6},$ $b=\\frac{11}{6},$ and \n\n$$\n\\frac{a}{b}=\\frac{(\\frac{17}{6})}{(\\frac{11}{6})}=\\frac{17}{11}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186414754 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "22215345-cf56-5cf6-8ec7-0d0ddc7f81fb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414754 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186414752 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414755 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186414754 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414755 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "74c122ae-6f5f-55d9-980e-db9851e51f87" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414755 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186414750 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414756 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186414755 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414756 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "84989845-fb61-500c-b47d-0a19bc3d185f" #edb/ref 